#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:1
msgid "llvm-objdump - LLVM's object file dumper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:8
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-objdump` \\[*commands*\\] \\[*options*\\] \\[*filenames...*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:12
msgid ""
"The {program}`llvm-objdump` utility prints the contents of object files and "
"final linked images named on the command line. If no file name is specified, "
"{program}`llvm-objdump` will attempt to read from *a.out*. If *-* is used as "
"a file name, {program}`llvm-objdump` will process a file on its standard "
"input stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:18
msgid "COMMANDS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:20
msgid ""
"At least one of the following commands are required, and some commands can "
"be combined with other commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:24
msgid "Display the information contained within an archive's headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:28
msgid ""
"Disassemble all executable sections found in the input files. On some "
"architectures (AArch64, PowerPC, x86), all known instructions are "
"disassembled by default. On the others, {option}`--mcpu` or {option}`--"
"mattr` is needed to enable some instruction sets. Disabled instructions are "
"displayed as `<unknown>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:36
msgid "Disassemble all sections found in the input files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:40
msgid ""
"Disassemble only the specified symbols. Takes demangled symbol names when "
"{option}`--demangle` is specified, otherwise takes mangled symbol names. "
"Implies {option}`--disassemble`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:44
msgid ""
"Each argument is split on commas. To select a symbol whose name contains "
"commas, use {option}`--disassemble` with a symbol argument instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:49
msgid ""
"Disassemble only the specified symbol. Takes a demangled symbol name when "
"{option}`--demangle` is specified, otherwise takes a mangled symbol name. "
"Implies {option}`--disassemble`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:53
msgid ""
"The argument is a single symbol name. To select multiple symbols, specify "
"this option multiple times or use {option}`--disassemble-symbols`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:58
msgid "Dump the specified DWARF debug sections. The supported values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:60
msgid "`frames` - .debug_frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:64
msgid "Display the contents of the overall file header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:68
msgid "Display the content of the fault map section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:72
msgid "Display summaries of the headers for each section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:76
msgid "Display usage information and exit. Does not stack with other commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:80
msgid "Display format-specific file headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:84
msgid "Display the relocation entries in the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:88
msgid "Display the dynamic relocation entries in the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:92
msgid "Dump the raw binary contents of the clang AST section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:96
msgid "Display the contents of each section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:100
msgid "Display the symbol table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:104
msgid "Display the contents of the dynamic symbol table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:108
msgid "Display the unwind info of the input(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:110
msgid ""
"This operation is only currently supported for COFF and Mach-O object files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:114
msgid ""
"Display the version of the {program}`llvm-objdump` executable. Does not "
"stack with other commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:119
msgid ""
"Display all available header information. Equivalent to specifying {option}"
"`--archive-headers`, {option}`--file-headers`, {option}`--private-headers`, "
"{option}`--reloc`, {option}`--section-headers`, and {option}`--syms`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:125
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:127
msgid "{program}`llvm-objdump` supports the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:130
msgid ""
"Increase the displayed address in disassembly or section header printing by "
"the specified offset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:135
msgid ""
"Specify the target architecture when disassembling. Use {option}`--version` "
"for a list of available targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:140
msgid ""
"Look up the object using the given build ID, specified as a hexadecimal "
"string. The found object is handled as if it were an input filename."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:145
msgid "Demangle symbol names in the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:149
msgid ""
"Provide a path to a directory with a `.build-id` subdirectory to search for "
"debug information for stripped binaries. Multiple instances of this argument "
"are searched in the order given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:155
msgid ""
"Distance to indent the source-level variable or inlined function display, "
"relative to the start of the disassembly. Defaults to 52 characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:160
msgid ""
"Print the locations of inlined functions alongside disassembly. `format` may "
"be `ascii`, `limits-only`, or `unicode`, defaulting to `unicode` if omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:166
msgid ""
"Print the locations (in registers or memory) of source-level variables "
"alongside disassembly. `format` may be `ascii` or `unicode`, defaulting to "
"`unicode` if omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:172
msgid ""
"Whether or not to try debuginfod lookups for debug binaries. Unless "
"specified, debuginfod is only enabled if libcurl was compiled in "
"(`LLVM_ENABLE_CURL`) and at least one server URL was provided by the "
"environment variable `DEBUGINFOD_URLS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:179
msgid ""
"Perform commands on the specified sections only. For Mach-O use `segment,"
"section` to specify the section name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:184
msgid ""
"When disassembling, display source line numbers. Implies {option}`--"
"disassemble`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:189
msgid "Pass target-specific disassembler options. Available options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:191
msgid ""
"`reg-names-std`: ARM only (default). Print in ARM 's instruction set "
"documentation, with r13/r14/r15 replaced by sp/lr/pc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:192
msgid "`reg-names-raw`: ARM only. Use r followed by the register number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:193
msgid ""
"`no-aliases`: AArch64 and RISC-V only. Print raw instruction mnemonic "
"instead of pseudo instruction mnemonic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:194
msgid ""
"`numeric`: RISC-V only. Print raw register names instead of ABI mnemonic. (e."
"g. print x1 instead of ra)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:195
msgid "`att`: x86 only (default). Print in the AT&T syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:196
msgid "`intel`: x86 only. Print in the intel syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:200
msgid "Enable or disable disassembler color output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:202
msgid "`off`: Disable disassembler color output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:203
msgid "`on`: Enable disassembler color output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:204
msgid ""
"`terminal`: Enable disassembler color output if the terminal supports it "
"(default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:208
msgid ""
"Target a specific CPU type for disassembly. Specify `--mcpu=help` to display "
"available CPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:213
msgid ""
"Enable/disable target-specific attributes. Specify `--mattr=help` to display "
"the available attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:218
msgid "Specify an argument to forward to LLVM's CommandLine library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:222
msgid ""
"When disassembling, do not print leading addresses for instructions or "
"inline relocations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:227
msgid "Do not use hex format for immediate values in disassembly output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:231
msgid "When disassembling, do not print the raw bytes of each instruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:235
msgid ""
"Display the content of the LLVM offloading sections and HIP offload bundles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:239
msgid ""
"When disassembling with the {option}`--source` option, prepend `prefix` to "
"absolute paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:244
msgid ""
"When disassembling with the {option}`--source` option, strip out `level` "
"initial directories from absolute paths. This option has no effect without "
"{option}`--prefix`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:250
msgid ""
"When disassembling with the {option}`--source` option, add `dir` to the "
"front of the source search path when looking up source files. For each "
"source file, llvm-objdump tries the path from the debug info, then each "
"search directory with the full path appended, then each search directory "
"with only the file name. This option may be specified multiple times; each "
"`--source-dir` adds one directory. Options on the command line are searched "
"in first to last order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:260
msgid ""
"When disassembling with the {option}`--source` option, replace `from` with "
"`to` at the start of the directory part of source file paths when looking up "
"sources. A rule is applied only if `from` ends at a directory separator in "
"the path. This option may be specified multiple times; rules are evaluated "
"in the order given and the first matching rule is used, as in GDB `set "
"substitute-path`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:269
msgid ""
"Use hex format when printing immediate values in disassembly output "
"(default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:273
msgid ""
"When disassembling, display source interleaved with the disassembly. Implies "
"{option}`--disassemble`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:278
msgid ""
"Show all symbols during disassembly, even if multiple symbols are defined at "
"the same location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:283
msgid ""
"Display the LMA column when dumping ELF section headers. Defaults to off "
"unless any section has different VMA and LMAs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:288
msgid "When disassembling, only disassemble from the specified address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:290
msgid ""
"When printing relocations, only print the relocations patching offsets from "
"at least `address`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:292
msgid ""
"When printing symbols, only print symbols with a value of at least `address`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:296
msgid ""
"When disassembling, only disassemble up to, but not including the specified "
"address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:298
msgid ""
"When printing relocations, only print the relocations patching offsets up to "
"`address`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:300
msgid "When printing symbols, only print symbols with a value up to `address`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:304
msgid ""
"When disassembling, symbolize a branch target operand to print a label "
"instead of a real address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:306
msgid ""
"When printing a PC-relative global symbol reference, print it as an offset "
"from the leading symbol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:308
msgid ""
"When a bb-address-map section is present (i.e., the object file is built "
"with `-fbasic-block-address-map`), labels are retrieved from that section "
"instead. If a pgo-analysis-map is present alongside the bb-address-map, any "
"available analyses are printed after the relevant block label. By default, "
"any analysis with a special representation (i.e. BlockFrequency, "
"BranchProbability, etc) are printed as raw hex values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:315
msgid ""
"Only supported for AArch64, BPF, PowerPC, RISC-V, and X86. Enabled by "
"default for BPF; use `--no-symbolize-operands` to disable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:318
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:320
msgid ""
"A non-symbolized branch instruction with a local target and pc-relative "
"memory access like"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:327
msgid "might become"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:337
msgid ""
"When using {option}`--symbolize-operands` with bb-address-map and pgo-"
"analysis-map, print analyses using the same format as their analysis passes "
"would. An example of pretty format would be printing block frequencies "
"relative to the entry block, the same as BFI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:342
msgid "Only works when {option}`--symbolize-operands` is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:346
msgid ""
"Target triple to disassemble for, see `--version` for available targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:350
msgid "Ignored for compatibility with GNU objdump."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:354
msgid ""
"Deprecated. When used with {option}`--disassemble`, choose style of code to "
"emit from X86 backend. Supported values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:359
msgid "AT&T-style assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:363
msgid "Intel-style assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:366
msgid "The default disassembly style is **att**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:370
msgid "Do not skip blocks of zeroes when disassembling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:374
msgid "Read command-line options and commands from response file `<FILE>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:377
msgid "MACH-O ONLY OPTIONS AND COMMANDS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:380
msgid ""
"Specify the architecture to disassemble. see `--version` for available "
"architectures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:385
msgid ""
"Print the offset to each archive member for Mach-O archives (requires "
"{option}`--archive-headers`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:390
msgid "Display binding info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:394
msgid "Display the data in code table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:398
msgid "Disassemble just the specified symbol's instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:402
msgid "Print chained fixup information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:406
msgid ""
"Print bind and rebase information used by dyld to resolve external "
"references in a final linked binary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:411
msgid "Display the shared libraries used for linked files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:415
msgid "Use .dSYM file for debug info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:419
msgid "Display the shared library's ID for dylib files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:423
msgid "Display exported symbols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:427
msgid ""
"Print the function starts table for Mach-O objects. Either `addrs` (default) "
"to print only the addresses of functions, `names` to print only the names of "
"the functions (when available), or `both` to print the names beside the "
"addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:434
msgid "Print line information from debug info if available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:438
msgid "Print the full leading address when disassembling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:442
msgid "Display the indirect symbol table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:446
msgid "Display the info plist section as strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:450
msgid "Display lazy binding info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-objdump.md:454
